[00:03.05] Hello darkness, my old friend
[00:07.62] I've come to talk with you again
[00:12.10] Because a vision softly creeping
[00:16.85] Left its seeds while I was sleeping
[00:21.21] And the vision that was planted in my brain
[00:28.07] Still remains
[00:31.11] Within the sound of silence
[00:36.97] In restless dreams, I walked alone
[00:41.88] Narrow streets of cobblestone
[00:46.39] 'Neath the halo of a streetlamp
[00:50.87] I turned my collar to the cold and damp
[00:55.40] When my eyes were stabbed by the flash of a neon light
[01:02.23] That split the night
[01:05.41] And touched the sound of silence
[01:11.31] And in the naked light, I saw
[01:16.08] Ten thousand people, maybe more
[01:20.71] People talking without speaking
[01:25.25] People hearing without listening
[01:29.45] People writing songs that voices never shared
[01:37.25] No one dared
[01:40.45] Disturb the sound of silence
[01:46.48] "Fools", said I, "You do not know
[01:50.92] Silence like a cancer grows
[01:55.12] Hear my words that I might teach you
[01:59.63] Take my arms that I might reach you"
[02:03.98] But my words like silent raindrops fell
[02:11.09] 
[02:13.13] And echoed in the wells of silence
[02:21.11] And the people bowed and prayed
[02:25.02] To the neon god they made
[02:29.33] And the sign flashed out its warning
[02:33.88] In the words that it was forming
[02:38.27] And the sign said, "The words of the prophets are written on the subway walls
[02:45.65] In tenement halls"
[02:48.89] And whispered in the sounds of silence
[02:56.76] 